          "explanation": "Most of the essays were first published in The Objectivist Newsletter, the periodical Rand and Branden edited in the early 1960s. The main exception is the opening essay, 'The Objectivist Ethics,' which began as Rand's 1961 lecture at a University of Wisconsin symposium. Academic journals is the tempting wrong answer, but professional philosophers largely ignored Rand at the time; her essays were written for an audience of admirers.",
