          "explanation": "Rand argued that ethics exists to guide the ordinary course of human life, in which people survive by thinking, producing, and trading. Emergencies suspend those conditions temporarily. Building morality around lifeboats, she said, teaches people to see life as catastrophe and others as perpetual victims. She did not say helping in emergencies is immoral -- she endorsed helping strangers when the risk to yourself is minimal.",
