          "explanation": "The straw-man charge says Rand defines altruism in its most extreme form -- that self-sacrifice is the moral ideal -- which few people actually hold. Ordinary morality asks you to weigh others' interests, not erase your own. If that middle position is coherent, Rand's either-or is a false dilemma. Hume's problem concerns deriving 'ought' from 'is,' and the robot objection concerns the foundation of value.",
