          "explanation": "The seminar approach is to steelman, then critique. Rand did not defend greed in the sense of grabbing by any means; she defended long-range, principled self-interest that forbids force and fraud and treats trade as the model. A fair reply states that, then names real objections -- Nozick's precondition gap, the is-ought problem, the false-dilemma charge, the hard cases. Cheerleading and dismissal both skip the thinking.",
